\title{Set literals in Disco}
\date{2026-02-19T19:27:48Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{We can write literal sets using curly braces and commas in between elements, just as in standard mathematical notation.  Notice that the order in which we write the elements, or the number of copies we write of each element, does not matter.}

\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> {1,2,3}
{1, 2, 3}
Disco> {3,1,1,2}
{1, 2, 3}
Disco> {}    -- this is how we write the empty set
{}
<<<

\p{We can also use [ellipses](https://disco-lang.readthedocs.io/en/latest/reference/ellipsis.html) to indicate an omitted sequence of elements.  Notice that the number of dots in the ellipses, or whether you use commas and/or spaces before and after the ellipses, does not matter.}

\pre\verb<<<|
Disco> {1..5}
{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
Disco> {1, ......., 5}
{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}
Disco> {1, 3, 5 ... 15}
{1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15}
Disco> {8, 7 ... 3}
{3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8}
Disco> {1, 4, 9, ... 36}
{1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36}<<<

